  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Lewis base: Chemical species which has capability to donate electron pair.</p><p>In <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>SF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>ClF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> central atom (i.e. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Cl</mi></math>)<br />having lone pair therefore act as Lewis base.</p><p>In <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>PCl</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;central atom <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mfenced></math> does not have lone pair therefore does not act as Lewis base.</p>",
